WEBVTT

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.070
Glaw!

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.070
Sciath!

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:41.250
Mordred... please...

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:43.060
Let's just...

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:45.770
Sagramore...

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:50.190
You seem ruthless at a glance, 
but in truth,

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.350
you care deeply for your friends.

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:03.910
I always thought that made you naïve.

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:10.460
N-No...

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:16.970
No!

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:53.060
<b>The Black Dragon Descends 
-Pen Draig-</b>

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:51.230
<i>"The Black Dragon Descends."</i>

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:56.310
<i>As the war dragged on into a quagmire,</i>

00:02:56.310 --> 00:03:00.990
<i>Queen Boudica collapsed, 
and the Knights-sorcerers were in crisis.</i>

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:05.470
<i>Meanwhile, Mordred revealed his true nature</i>

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:10.810
<i>and killed Sagramore right in front of Ocoho, 
while Seth, unaware of all this,</i>

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:15.220
<i>was facing off one-on-one with Dragunov.</i>

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:22.340
Sorry you didn't even get a moment 
to enjoy your reunion,

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:25.100
but I'll need you to come with me.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.610
Like hell I will!

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:30.610
Why did you have to start this war?!

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.240
The Inquisition wants to

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:43.110
reclaim the authority it lost 
during the incident in Rumble Town!

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:46.490
That's why we went along 
with the Merchant Barons' plan!

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:49.210
The Merchant Barons?

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:51.250
The guys who chased me around?

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:55.670
The schemes of a great many people 
are driving this war.

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:59.130
You can't stop it with your fists 
the way you stopped Konrad!

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:02.800
Then I'll just bust all of them up

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.290
and stop this war!

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:09.270
You said her name was Melie?

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:15.820
Spare a thought for the position 
you're currently in,

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:19.280
before you race ahead 
without considering the consequences.

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:20.780
You...

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:23.190
Listen to me.

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:27.160
You and I are going to stop the war.

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:33.660
Where'd that little brat go?

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.180
And she had the gall 
to make fun of my outfit!

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.860
Gosh, she just won't give up!

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:43.550
Maybe I provoked her a bit too much.

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:59.940
Did you think you could 
get away from me twice?

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:05.420
Darting around won't save you.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:09.330
There is no escape from my sword!

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:11.760
Rolling strike!

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.110
Graceful defense!

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.400
In that case, double thrust!

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:15.410
Triple counter!

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:16.750
Spit-roasting screw!

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.390
Splendid!

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:21.300
What an honor to fight a master like you!

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.400
Happy to hear it!

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:24.560
You are quite skilled yourself!

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:25.760
If we had met...

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:26.880
...under different circumstances...

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:28.390
...we may have been...

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:30.070
Don't finish that sentence!

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:31.640
Such is the nature of war!

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:33.640
So true! The fate of the swordsman!

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.890
Indeed! And since it's come to this...

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:38.020
Our blades will do the talking!

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:38.900
Come!

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:39.770
Showdown!

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:41.520
Time to settle this!

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:45.780
Sagramore!

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:47.530
Sagramore!

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:49.780
Sagramore!

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:51.790
My goodness.

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:55.690
It's not easy to get blood 
out of such fine wood, you know.

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:57.710
Sorry about that, Dad.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:59.590
Mordred!

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:02.850
Why did you keep quiet 
about this all these years?

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:04.590
We've been your friends 
since we were kids!

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:09.260
It doesn't seem that 
this shrew will ever join our side.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:12.300
She outlived her usefulness long ago.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:15.490
Then take care of her at once.

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:18.810
It's time to set sail 
for the Ponantin countries.

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:24.940
Mordred...

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:27.870
All those times you helped me before...

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:30.850
Even when I was about to be stripped 
of my knighthood,

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:32.680
and you stood up for me...

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:34.450
Was it all a lie?

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:38.100
I needed to keep you by my side.

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:40.390
I did it to protect you.

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:44.590
Isn't that what I told you? 
Of course, that wasn't a lie.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:48.340
If I had been separated from you,

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:51.220
all my hard work would have 
gone to waste, after all.

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:54.210
Making use of your curse

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:56.350
was the cornerstone of this plan.

00:06:58.030 --> 00:07:01.100
Do you have no regrets at all?

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.570
Regrets?

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:05.680
No, none.

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:08.360
I don't feel anything at all, you see.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.260
That is my curse.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:13.620
I have no emotions.

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:17.240
You never noticed, did you?

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:21.370
I was pretending, 
based on the way you two acted.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.160
Sagramore was a big help.

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:27.880
Being next to his stern face

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:31.420
actually made me look 
as though I had feelings.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:34.020
Just look.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:37.310
He looks far more expressive 
now than before.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:39.180
Mordred!

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:41.450
Don't get all worked up.

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:43.190
Let's end this now.

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:45.900
Your part in this is over.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:49.070
Sheesh...

00:07:50.930 --> 00:07:51.820
Draccoon!

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:54.070
No...

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:55.820
Stay with me!

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:57.830
Draccoon!

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:00.510
That's enough, Mordred.

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:02.970
I told you, that's fine wood.

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:04.830
I'm sorry, Dad.

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:08.930
Mordred... How low can you stoop?!

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:11.840
Jump off of this ship.

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:32.490
Did you mean it? Can we really 
stop this war if I go with you?

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:35.740
Stay alert. 
We're approaching the front lines.

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:51.130
What is all this?

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:56.360
The Inquisition would go this far?

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:57.260
It can't be true!

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:00.130
Unfortunately, it is true.

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:04.640
And the Merchant Barons have 
an even more hideous plan.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:06.460
What more can they do?

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:09.980
They're going to enslave all of the infected.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:11.150
What?!

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:14.410
Why are you going along 
with a plan like that?!

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:16.380
Even you should know that's wrong!

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:18.910
General Torque has a just cause in mind.

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:21.290
And I have faith in it.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:23.410
Did you say... "Torque"?

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:30.500
He's... That bastard is...

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:33.100
What kind of "just cause" could he have?!

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:36.130
All they ever do is make sorcerers suffer!

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:38.570
I understand your anger,

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:42.130
but the world is not that simple.

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:43.520
What?!

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:45.160
Listen.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:49.130
It's none other than the 
Inquisition that protects people

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:51.190
from infected evildoers.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:57.450
Not all the infected in this world 
are worthy of pity.

00:09:57.450 --> 00:10:01.200
We need an organization 
that can protect the powerless.

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:06.350
This greater cause of yours...

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:09.330
Is it really something 
you've thought about for yourself?

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:16.310
I want to stop this miserable war.

00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:19.840
That is, without a doubt, 
my own thought.

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:24.850
I can trust you, right?

00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:27.030
You'll know soon enough.

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:35.070
That's the signal!

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:37.740
The horned sorcerer has been captured!

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:42.380
Cease fire!

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:47.500
They've stopped attacking!

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:49.500
What was that signal, anyway?

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:52.150
Who fired the signal shot?

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:53.950
Look! That kid!

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:56.130
He looks just like that Spectre!

00:10:56.450 --> 00:10:58.370
How dare you destroy our land!

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:01.000
You crushed my grandfather's field!

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:02.890
Get out of here! Drop dead!

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:05.110
You ugly, horned menace!

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:11.320
You have a response to everything I say,

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:14.270
but you let them say whatever they want?

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:17.030
What good would it do to argue?

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:22.170
When that happened, you did everything 
you could to minimize the damage.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:23.670
Didn't you?

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:26.980
That's right.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:30.790
But in the end, I still caused damage.

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.920
They have every right to be angry.

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:37.170
If I were in their place, 
I'd be just as furious.

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:39.670
You...

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:43.390
I knew we could count on Captain Dragunov.

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:47.940
The little lost lamb has safely found 
its way to us.

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:49.680
Signal the ships.

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:53.950
That's the signal! Assume formation!

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.570
What's going on?

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:00.260
What are they doing?

00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:02.950
What's all the noise for?

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:05.070
It's...

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:22.090
What is that?

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:25.830
That's the flagship of Bome...

00:12:25.830 --> 00:12:27.780
The great battleship, Uranos!

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:29.810
Why is it here?

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:33.100
At last, it is time!

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:37.210
I feel this war could have 
gone on far longer,

00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:41.140
but let us at least ensure 
that it goes out with a bang!

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:43.990
On my beard!

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:49.990
<b>[Battle Airship Uranos] 
Uranos is the flagship of the Inquisition's home country of Bome. 
It rules the skies as the symbol of a merciless judgment.</b>

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:10.230
It's bombing the castle!

00:13:10.230 --> 00:13:12.020
We have to hurry back!

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:26.650
A child?

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:45.010
Now the magic barrier around the castle 
will fall within minutes!

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:49.550
On my beard, 
I couldn't be more excited!

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:53.810
What a thrill to witness 
the demise of a kingdom!

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:59.440
Dear queen, I hope you're enjoying 
this glorious spectacle, as well!

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:05.570
Hey, eyepatch! 
Weren't they supposed to stop their attack?!

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:07.830
Is this what you were after?!

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:11.580
Did you trick me 
so you could destroy everything?!

00:14:12.110 --> 00:14:13.220
No...

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:19.050
Just as planned, 
Cyfandir will now fall.

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:23.590
The Inquisition will reclaim its former glory,

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:27.230
and with our conquest of this land 
as the first case,

00:14:27.230 --> 00:14:30.590
the world will be kept under ironclad order.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.450
Dragunov...

00:14:35.170 --> 00:14:40.230
I know you understand very well 
what is right.

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:48.240
I am aware that you have your misgivings 
about this mission.

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:53.560
And they are not only about
 the horned sorcerer's capture.

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:58.660
You are concerned about our military 
intervention in Cyfandir, are you not?

00:14:58.980 --> 00:14:59.920
Yes, sir.

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:01.620
Do not worry.

00:15:02.190 --> 00:15:06.850
My only desire is to reclaim 
the ironclad order we once had.

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:10.340
It is my wish to shed 
as little blood as possible.

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:12.140
General Torque...

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:15.560
I wanted to trust him.

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:18.610
What was all that about stopping the war?!

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:19.810
This is a betrayal!

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:22.810
Yes... I've been betrayed.

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:25.310
Don't make this all about you!

00:15:25.310 --> 00:15:26.690
Make them stop attacking!

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:29.090
I don't have the authority to do that.

00:15:29.090 --> 00:15:32.070
Is that so?! Then I'm outta here!

00:15:32.690 --> 00:15:33.700
Where are you going?

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:37.450
To beat the hell out of the guy 
who's doing this!

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:41.090
You're going to race off again
without thinking about the consequences?

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:46.840
You told me to think 
before I took off running.

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:49.780
But if that's going to end in regrets,

00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:52.720
I'll choose to run 
as many times as I have to!

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:04.170
Look! The enemy!

00:16:04.170 --> 00:16:05.980
Th-The horned sorcerer!

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:09.500
Skull Attack!

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:17.300
Keep going until you're at the center 
of the battlefield.

00:16:17.300 --> 00:16:19.580
That's where Santori is.

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:21.330
Eyepatch...

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:24.350
Be careful. He's strong.

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:26.820
But while he's moving,

00:16:26.820 --> 00:16:29.150
he can make only one part 
of his body larger at a time.

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:30.960
Find it.

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:32.220
You...

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:35.590
Why are you still hanging around here?! 
Get going!

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:37.460
Run!

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:43.480
What's the meaning of this, 
Captain Dragunov?

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:46.480
The Inquisition has no just cause.

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:51.110
Outrageous! 
And you call yourself a Thaumaturge—

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:58.230
You guys are here, too?

00:16:58.230 --> 00:17:02.120
Our loyalty is to you at all times, Captain.

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:04.870
Just leave things here to us!

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:09.000
We'll show you 
how much stronger we are now!

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:11.970
We've gotten pretty good 
at cooking, too!

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:18.140
Is that so? I guess I was the 
only one stuck in one place.

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:19.140
Huh?

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:21.140
All right, men!

00:17:21.550 --> 00:17:25.140
As of this moment, 
we'll be acting independently.

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:28.820
Yes, it's a path 
that won't get us very far ahead.

00:17:28.820 --> 00:17:30.110
But you don't mind, right?

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:30.860
Yes, sir!

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:38.650
Goodbye, Ocoho.

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:46.000
Draccoon?

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:49.500
You found me in the Sidh?

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:55.200
Pulling won't do any good.

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:59.140
I'm completely under 
Mordred's control right now.

00:18:01.690 --> 00:18:04.440
Are you trying to take me back?

00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:07.380
Wait... I'm moving on my own?

00:18:08.090 --> 00:18:09.400
How?

00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:12.400
A lingering trace of Gysoni?

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:16.080
I get it! It was never undone!

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:19.690
And you used that to bring 
my senses back to me?

00:18:23.980 --> 00:18:25.040
Huh?

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:27.540
Draccoon!

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:29.170
Huh?

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:32.380
Draccoon! Don't leave me!

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:33.180
You're still here?

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:36.170
I ordered you to jump off the ship.

00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:39.940
Oh? You're back to your senses?

00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:41.220
Well, that's a problem.

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:45.350
I'll have to get the deck messy 
and get yelled at by Dad again.

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:47.980
Careful. She's a reckless one.

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:49.480
Shut up.

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:52.130
Ocoho, you get it, don't you?

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:53.980
It's all over.

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:56.840
Just act like the puppet you are,

00:18:56.840 --> 00:18:59.530
and let me manipulate you as I please.

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:00.660
Shut up!

00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:04.910
Do that, and out of respect for our 
past relationship, I'll give you a painless—

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:06.150
Shut up!

00:19:06.150 --> 00:19:08.540
You were manipulating me all along!

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:12.880
Well, now it's your turn to be the puppet!

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:14.170
Gysoni!

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:30.310
I need to get out of this hole 
before the magic barrier falls.

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:35.850
Stop trying so hard.

00:19:35.850 --> 00:19:39.570
You people are infected. 
That means you're sick.

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:42.330
"Sick," you say?

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:45.460
That's right.

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:49.330
And we're kindly offering to take care of you.

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:53.410
You can't beat me just by defending, anyway.

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:55.840
No? Then...

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:58.340
How about if I do this?!

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:03.090
You seem pretty hopeless in close quarters!

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:04.470
<i>What happened?!</i>

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:07.100
<i>Her posture, her eyes, her fighting style...</i>

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:09.340
<i>Everything about her has changed!</i>

00:20:09.340 --> 00:20:11.540
<i>It's as if she's a different person!</i>

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:15.760
You have broken formation.

00:20:15.760 --> 00:20:17.230
What's going on?

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:19.620
C-Colonel Santori!

00:20:19.620 --> 00:20:23.110
Somehow, the horned sorcerer is running free!

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:24.610
What?!

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:30.620
H-He's heading straight for us!

00:20:32.030 --> 00:20:34.630
This is what you'd call 
a perfect opportunity!

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:36.700
After being so disillusioned by the queen,

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:41.010
a one-on-one with the horned boy 
is exactly what I want!

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:42.050
Here he comes!

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:44.260
You won't get any closer!

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:45.510
Skull Burst!

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:48.870
On my beard!

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:51.770
It's raining soldiers!

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:55.770
Are you coming from that way, 
little brat?!

00:20:58.690 --> 00:20:59.770
Pulsar!

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:05.680
How delightful!

00:21:05.680 --> 00:21:10.370
You have improved significantly 
in the short time since I last saw you!

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:13.230
How many were lost?

00:21:13.230 --> 00:21:16.250
About 30% of our soldiers 
were lost in that attack.

00:21:17.890 --> 00:21:21.420
What about the queen? 
Shouldn't we send someone to rescue her?

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:23.290
The rain is hiding her from us!

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:26.250
Then we'll form a rescue team 
to save her!

00:21:26.250 --> 00:21:28.490
Half of you, follow me!

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:29.650
Wait!

00:21:29.650 --> 00:21:31.860
There's Fantasia of unknown origin

00:21:31.860 --> 00:21:34.260
coming from the direction 
of the castle at high speeds!

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:35.350
What?!

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:37.660
It's several times faster than a dragon.

00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:39.650
No, even faster than that!

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:40.610
Impossible!

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:43.740
It will reach us in mere moments!

00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:51.990
Could that be the great Merlin's...

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:56.410
The celestial shoe!

00:22:05.800 --> 00:22:07.300
What the?!

00:22:07.300 --> 00:22:09.300
What in the world...

00:22:20.610 --> 00:22:25.990
Seth! Get me out of this thing!

00:22:24.980 --> 00:22:28.890
D-Doc?!

00:22:25.990 --> 00:22:29.990
To Be Continued

00:24:00.020 --> 00:24:20.700
<b>Next Time</b>

00:24:00.550 --> 00:24:03.040
<i>The mysterious warrior 
who has landed on the battlefield</i>

00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:05.620
<i>is Doc, merged with a suit of armor.</i>

00:24:06.150 --> 00:24:10.010
<i>A new enemy, Verone of the Inquisition, 
stands before him,</i>

00:24:10.980 --> 00:24:14.700
<i>and Seth enters the final battle with Santori.</i>

00:24:15.330 --> 00:24:20.020
<i>Seth's rage explodes 
against the strongest and most evil of foes!</i>

00:24:20.020 --> 00:24:24.500
<i>Next time on <i>Radiant</i>, 
"The Will of the People Shines Bright."</i>

00:24:20.700 --> 00:24:25.020
<b>The Will of the People Shines Bright 
-Resistance-</b>

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.250
<b>Next time, the final battle!</b>

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.250
<b>Help me!</b>

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.250
<b>End</b>
